# SABOTAGE: D-13 (ADR-048 §6/§8, operator ruling D-13) — the BUDGET re-check at the LEVEL 2
# RETRY boundary is REMOVED from `Samen.AI.Agent.complete_with_recovery/10`. This is the
# 322 shape for the THIRD of the turn boundary's three guards: 322 removes the kill-switch
# re-check at that boundary, 323 removes the durable cancel check one level down inside
# `derive_fold/8`, and THIS removes the budget one — so a run that exhausted the allowance
# its tenant set DURING the overflowing attempt is silently ignored. Level 2 derives a fold,
# ships the tenant's folded conversation to the provider for summarization (a REAL governed
# provider call since C3, and D4 is explicit that it SPENDS the run's token allowances and
# its wall-clock one) and then spends a SECOND provider call on the retry, noticing the
# overrun only at the NEXT turn boundary. That is a knowing overrun of a tenant budget.
#
# Flips the named D-13 red. Everything else stays GREEN, which is what makes the red mean
# what it says: the D-13 POSITIVE CONTROL (the byte-identical script WITHIN budget, whose
# Level 2 fold IS recorded model-written and whose retry DOES happen) still passes, and so
# do the P5 red, the P5 positive control and all three D-05 arms — so the red fails because
# the BUDGET re-check is gone, not because Level 2, the summarizer, or the budget predicate
# itself broke.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: `over_budget/2` and the TURN-boundary budget terminal it feeds
# (sabotage 240 owns that), the kill-switch clause immediately above (322 owns it), D-05's
# cancel check inside `derive_fold/8` (323 owns it), the closed `@error_kinds` literal, and
# C2's Level 2 bound — the `attempt <= @max_context_retries and context_overflow?(result)`
# clause with its `derive_fold/8` call, its recursion, its `{:halt, ...}` arm and the
# `true ->` arm are all left exactly as they are.
#
# Deletes ONE CONTIGUOUS `cond` clause and its comment, replacing it with a `# SABOTAGE`
# comment, so the file still compiles under `--warnings-as-errors` (an `if false do` shape
# would trip Elixir's always-same-result warning). No private function goes uncalled:
# `over_budget/2` is public and still called at the turn boundary, and `reload!/1` keeps its
# other callers. Touches agent.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_durability_test.exs
